# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# secrets
#
# .env holds the bot token, which is full control of the bot account, plus the
# channel id, owner id and any paid RPC key. .env.example is the committed
# template and is the ONLY .env* file that may be tracked.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# runtime state
#
# The settings table lives in SQLite, so a committed DB would ship someone
# else's thresholds and watchlist. In Docker this is a named volume at
# /data/dipbot.sqlite; locally it is ./data/.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
*.db
*-backup-*.sqlite
*.log


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# spike artifacts
#
# Recorded ticks, discovered vaults and scale-test logs from spike/. Several MB
# of live-market recordings that only mean anything alongside the run that made
# them. tests/fixtures/ticks.jsonl is the curated replay corpus and IS tracked -
# tests/test_replay.py fails without it, so never widen these into a bare
# *.jsonl rule.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
spike/data/
spike/tokens.json
spike/vaults.json
spike/other_dexes.json


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.venv/
venv/
env/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.Python


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# test & tooling caches
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
.tox/


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AI assistant context
#
# Working notes for coding agents, not part of the project. Kept local so the
# published repo carries only its own documentation. Nothing in dipbot/ or
# tests/ reads any of these, so ignoring them changes no behaviour.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
CLAUDE.md
CLAUDE.local.md
AGENTS.md
.claude/
.cursor/
.cursorrules
.windsurfrules
.aider*
.github/copilot-instructions.md


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# editors & OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~
